{
  "_readme": [
    "How each beer is poured. The card beside the glass turns every few seconds,",
    "and when a beer comes to rest the glass is tuned to its entry here.",
    "",
    "Keys beginning with an underscore are notes, not settings — the renderers",
    "skip them. Everything else is a slider in the tuning panel and means what",
    "that slider means.",
    "",
    "_style, _abv and _ibu are the beer's own: ABV and IBU are printed on the",
    "label art in beers/, and the style is either printed there too or taken",
    "from the brewery's Untappd and MyBeer listings, which _from records.",
    "Five entries also carry photo, meaning the colour was measured off a real",
    "glass of it in samples/beers rather than chosen for the style.",
    "",
    "The numbers follow from the style, then bend to the beer: lacing rises",
    "with IBU, and body, opacity and colour depth rise with ABV. So the two",
    "hazy IPAs at 20 and 25 IBU are near neighbours, and the 70 IBU red IPA",
    "laces the glass in a way the 7 IBU sour never will.",
    "",
    "clarity and caustics are read by the shader version only."
  ],
